[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ipni-maturity-iteration-01", :doc/title "IPNI maturity — Co-Scientist iteration 01", :doc/path "90-docs/ipni_maturity/iteration-01.edn", :source/dataset "ipni-maturity", :doc/measured-at "2026-08-20T06:56:50Z", :doc/score 36.36363636363635, :doc/body "# IPNI maturity — Co-Scientist iteration 01\n\n> Judge: `ipni-maturity.audit` over `ipni-maturity.probe` — measured HTTP\n> statuses and manifest facts, no LLM. Ranking: `kaizen.elo`, round-robin,\n> the measured gain is the judge.\n>\n> Probed 2026-08-20T06:56:50Z. 100.00% of the rubric was measurable; nothing was unmeasurable, so nothing is excluded.\n\n## Score\n\n**36.36 / 100**\n\n## Findings (heaviest recoverable headroom first)\n\n| axis | weight | finding |\n|---|---|---|\n| `discoverable-as-provider` | 0.2 | a CID kotobase serves resolves to third-party providers only — kotobase is not among them |\n| `chain-published` | 0.18 | no advertisement chain has ever been published — /ipni/v1/head is 404 |\n| `advertise-wired` | 0.15 | zero call sites for ipni.advertise/announce/ad/head anywhere in the workspace |\n| `publisher-identity` | 0.13 | no publisher identity: manifest/ipni-publisher.edn does not name a peer id, and cid.contact rejects an announce whose address carries no /p2p/{peer-id} |\n| `dependency-declared` | 0.08 | io-ipni-specs is not a declared dependency of anything — the library is unreachable from any deployed code |\n| `entries-hamt` | 0.03 | ipni.hamt returns :not-yet-implemented — honest, but caps an advertisement at one EntryChunk |\n\n## Roadmap (Elo)\n\n| Elo | id | axis | startable? | observable? | +gain |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1273 | `ipni-h1` | `discoverable-as-provider` | no — publisher identity — manifest/ipni-publisher.edn names no peer id | yes | +16.53 |\n| 1244 | `ipni-h2` | `chain-published` | no — publisher identity — manifest/ipni-publisher.edn names no peer id | yes | +14.88 |\n| 1215 | `ipni-h3` | `advertise-wired` | no — publisher identity — an advertisement needs a signed Provider | yes | +12.40 |\n| 1186 | `ipni-h4` | `publisher-identity` | no — an owner decision, not a task: which identity kotobase publishes under | yes | +10.74 |\n| 1156 | `ipni-h5` | `dependency-declared` | yes | no | +6.61 |\n| 1126 | `ipni-h6` | `entries-hamt` | yes | no | +2.48 |\n\n## Meta\n\n**Every member of the startable batch is unobservable from outside.**\n\nShipping all of it moves the score **+6.61** (to 42.98 / 100) without changing anything a\nstranger can see. That is the same defect as an unmeasured metric wearing the\nopposite mask, so this iteration does not bank the gain: it reports the blocked\nwork instead.\n\nThe three highest-Elo hypotheses share one blocker:\n\n- publisher identity — manifest/ipni-publisher.edn names no peer id\n- publisher identity — an advertisement needs a signed Provider\n- an owner decision, not a task: which identity kotobase publishes under\n\nThat is a decision, not a task. Until it is made, IPNI maturity is capped at 42.98 / 100 and every point of the remainder is behind it.\n\n## Method note\n\nThree earlier versions of the probe swept `orgs/` directly for call sites; on 4,400\ncheckouts none finished, and each reported the two heaviest axes as `:unknown`. The\nworking version derives them instead: a namespace cannot be required without its\ndependency on the classpath, so zero declarations across 4218 repos (3480 manifests read) implies zero call\nsites. The evidence floor is reported so 0 hits cannot be read as 0 looked at.\n"}]